<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    AI cross-level jumping (§83b).

    Hung off vanilla's OWN modder insertion hook rather than patched into the Humanlike tree
    by XPath: ThinkNode_SubtreesByTag splices every ThinkTreeDef declaring the matching
    insertTag, so this adds a node without touching a vanilla def and cannot collide with
    another mod doing the same thing.

    Humanlike_PostDuty is the correct tag and the choice is load-bearing, not cosmetic. A pawn
    only reaches it once its Lord duty subtree has produced NO job - so "the AI wanted to get
    somewhere and could not" is a structural fact at this point in the tree instead of a
    heuristic we would otherwise have to invent and tune. An ordinary raid, where the duty
    works, never runs a line of this.
  -->
  <ThinkTreeDef>
    <defName>AB2_BandLeap</defName>
    <insertTag>Humanlike_PostDuty</insertTag>
    <insertPriority>50</insertPriority>
    <thinkRoot Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <li Class="AsAboveSoBelow.JobGiver_ABBandLeap" />
      </subNodes>
    </thinkRoot>
  </ThinkTreeDef>

</Defs>
